49	122	\N	2023-12-16 12:39:04.433	63.33	[{"id": 1, "kind": "122", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/1/52/SESSION_122_1.pdf", "size": null, "shown": true, "status": null, "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": null, "dateUpload": "17-05-2024 12:12:31", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Dissertation Anglais.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	<p>----Begin</p>\n<p>Artificial Intelligence has been an issue of heated debates during the last decade. It is considered to be as a breakthrough in the word of technology that flipped out all of the concepts in the business organisations world.Some consider that&nbsp; AI-based systems influenced lots of aspects such as work force demographics, meaningfulness of jobs, employer-employee relationship and a lot more , others believe that AI-based systems are the creation of humain beings so these systems will always be totally controlled by humans and it's up to them to choose the impact of these systems on the business organisations . In addition to these two groups , there is a group of people that believe that AI-based systems have an impact on the business organisations but at a certain extent.</p>\n<p>AI-based systems significantly transformed aspects of business organisations and these aspects will never be again the same , some jobs now can completly be replaced by machines , people use this technologies as a way to give them answers without having to think ,let's take the example of chatgpt which is natural language system that provides the possibility of writing emails , correcting grammar mistakes and even translating texts to other languages , the world will never&nbsp; be the same after the invasion of these technologies.</p>\n<p>On the other hand&nbsp; some consider that AI-based systems are all human creation so all of the impacts are choson by human beings and believe strongly that these machines or technology will never replace the presence of humans or even impact business organisations if humans don't allow it , it's up to humans to decide where and when and how these technologies are emerged or used in business organisations .</p>\n<p>A third group , believe that the emergence of AI-based systems in the business organisations will have an impact at a certain extent , machines can not get into or transform human relashionships for example the employer and employee relashionship but in some&nbsp; cases could replace the human beings in the excution of some tasks .</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>There is no doubt that AI-based systems significantly transformed aspects of business organisations. Three points where presented here which are that these systems impact business organisations for others it is always the impact of human beings and for a third group it is at a certain extent but where is AI planning for us for the next years.</p>	SOUMETTRE	\N	2
5	122	\N	2023-12-16 12:38:36.782	6.33	[{"id": 1, "kind": "122", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/1/7/SESSION_122_1.pdf", "size": null, "shown": true, "status": null, "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": null, "dateUpload": "17-05-2024 12:19:51", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Dissertation Anglais.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	<p>The emergence of AI-based systems in the business model will transform a demograhic model, nature and employer-employee relationship.</p>\n<p>Our environment in a dynamic cycle and competitive experience</p>	SOUMETTRE	\N	2
