rvesting the digital green A deeper look at the sustainable revolution brought by next generation IoT in E Commerce.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}, {"id": 6, "kind": "22", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/1/35/SESSION_22_6.pdf", "size": "191.13 kb", "shown": true, "status": "SOUMETTRE", "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": "19-02-2024 21:11:14", "dateUpload": "19-02-2024 05:07:58", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "La digitalisation au service de la durabilité en Tunisie  Abstract.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}, {"id": 7, "kind": "22", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/1/35/SESSION_22_7.pdf", "size": "113.37 kb", "shown": true, "status": "SOUMETTRE", "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": "19-02-2024 21:11:14", "dateUpload": "19-02-2024 05:07:58", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Le rôle de la transformation digitale dans l’implémentation des Objectifs du Développement Durable  Cas de la Tunisie.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}, {"id": 8, "kind": "22", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/1/35/SESSION_22_8.pdf", "size": "386.2 kb", "shown": true, "status": "SOUMETTRE", "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": "19-02-2024 21:11:14", "dateUpload": "19-02-2024 05:07:58", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "RSE et Entreprises entre adoption et méfiance.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	\N	SOUMETTRE	\N	\N
111	122	\N	2024-12-23 12:19:42.786	68.50	[{"id": 1, "kind": "122", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/2\\\\154\\\\SESSION_122_1.pdf", "size": null, "shown": true, "status": null, "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": null, "dateUpload": "24-02-2025 20:43:12", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Dissertation Anglais.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	<p style="text-align: justify;">Smartphones have revolutionized the way we interact with the word around us, some people think that it has many advanteges and helps us to facilitate communication between familymembers ,friends and colleagues,... Others belive that it has many disadvanteges and it impactes badly our lifes and relationships. So, are we consider samrtphones as tools to interact with the word or the main of our daily lives? We will discuss the two points of view , we will start with the advantages then the disadvantages.<br><br></p>\n<p style="text-align: justify;">First, we can't neglicte the fact that smartphones have revolutionized the way we interact with the word around us, embodying a convergence of communication , information and entertainment tools: this object make the communication easier between people all over the word . Today we don't have to wait until someone go to the office or the house so we can call him , we have phones in our hands all the day so with a simple clic we can interact with our target. Also, this technologie tool makes us able to find the information that we are searching for easily , consulting news and reciving it .Second&nbsp; , with the birth of games, socail media and recently IA , the smartphone is concedered as an entertainment tool so we can play divers games , scroll the different social media plateform and discuss with our friends easily.&nbsp; In addition, phones , by the time , are innovated so they can replace books , PCs , and other tools so we can buy it and use it for seviral contextes.<br><br>However , their pervasive presence in our daily lives raises concerns about how much they can manipulate us and our relationships: we can remarque that in our daily life we use smartphones 90% of the time ; communicating , working ,&nbsp; scrolling , chating ,.. that make us say that we all all addicted to this magical tool. 10 years earlier , only teenagers or adulters were using it but owerdays even our parents grand parents are addicted and use it for seviral cases and situations. Forther more , using phones is the main reason for some deases espacilly for kids like obesity , authisme ,.. Last , we can also say that this phenemonal tool , is impacting the way of communication and the relationships: if we watch a simple family at the dinner table we can notice that there is no real communication they are all watching their screens and eat . Even in the profesionnal context , employees use their phone while working because of their addiction and it's decrease the productivity and the concentration. Last but not least , because the exponential use of this tool , the soft skills of people , students , employees ,.. are badly inpacted so they can prefer working from home and communicate behind a screen.</p>\n<p style="text-align: justify;">In conclusion , smartphones are a good tools to be used for many reasons , but we need to take care and controle this use so we can live without it .&nbsp;</p>\n<p style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style="text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</p>	SOUMETTRE	\N	2
35	122	\N	2023-12-16 12:36:37.698	75.00	[{"id": 1, "kind": "122", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/1/38/SESSION_122_1.pdf", "size": null, "shown": true, "status": null, "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": null, "dateUpload": "17-05-2024 11:45:31", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Dissertation Anglais.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	<p>Thousands of poeple start integrated AI-based systems in their lifes. OpenAI solutions are mostly adopted by more than eight thousands users. The industry 4.0 is considered as a revolution in the business organisations. It represents a debate nowadays. AI-based applications or approaches are integrated in many domains ans especially industries.</p>\n<p>Group of poeple see that AI-based systems are helping campanies to get better performance without affecting employability or customer experience. A second group in convainced that IA-based technology is destroying the human relationships and reducing the work force demographics.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Those how believe that AI-based systems are benific for our economy are based on the rapidity of production. They believe that if such a technology exist, there is no need to waste time and human effort on realizing tasks that can be done by robots for example. Forthemore, the relationship between employee and employer depends on the behave of everyone them but not on how AI can resolve their technical problems.</p>\n<p>From another point of view, another group see that AI-based solutions are represnting a danger. ArtificAIl intelligence and smart robots are replacing humans in many area of work. This can directly affect the number of workers. Thus, slowly the work foce demography is decreasing and poeple will loose their jobs. The business production sector will loose the taste of creativity. Thus, every product will be reproduced without being customized.&nbsp; Technology is replacing humans.</p>\n<p>A third group find that AI-based solutions are dangerous if it is not controlled. The business organizations must study the choice of integrating AI-based systems or not. They have to choose when and where integrating it. An important question must be answered: What value can be added by this AI solution? If it replaces employees, it can make exactly their work? What is the cost of installing it?&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If these questions are answered correctly, the organization can take the white choice. AI-based solutions can replace automatic tasks but cannot replace human brains and human creativity.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The emergence of Artificial Intelligence leads to a better performance of many business organisations. At the same time, it affect the working state. If it becomes an automated integration it can lead to a significant transformation of all human life ecosystem. If so, what can humans do when AI robots replace their work?</p>	SOUMETTRE	\N	2
