109	122	\N	2024-12-23 12:47:54.185	58.00	[{"id": 1, "kind": "122", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/2\\\\158\\\\SESSION_122_1.pdf", "size": null, "shown": true, "status": null, "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": null, "dateUpload": "24-02-2025 10:05:50", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Dissertation Anglais.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	<p>The use of smartphones presents both advantages and disavantages. In the first hand, according to a new statistic, more than 50% of people around the world are connected using a smartphone.</p>\n<p>It can be a quick tool to have informations, like weather for the next hours or days, national and international exclusive news, and past and future events.</p>\n<p>In professional environments, a smartphone can be a tool for interviews and meetings, it help us to communicate at any place and each time.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Specialy, in universities, more than 90% of students are connected. Smartphones help them to communicate each other, and to change documents and informations with their teachers. Using the applications and tools in classroom can improve their background, by searching definitions, examples and exercices.</p>\n<p>However, the excessive use of smarphones has a negative impact in our health. The pervasive presence of intelligent tools like smartphones, in our daily lives, can decrease the benefits of face to face changes, and increase the isolation of persons, which is a signification of addiction.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>A new study demonstrate that 45% of students connected in classroom with social media apps, lost their concentration and miss some important remarks and futur homeworks given by their teachers.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Therefore, in our daily live, we should make a crucial balance to increase the benefits of using smartphones, and to decrease their disavantages.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>	SOUMETTRE	\N	2
