95	122	\N	2024-12-23 12:39:36.136	80.50	[{"id": 1, "kind": "122", "path": "/mnt/core-data/appfiles/pgpg/uploadedFiles/2\\\\162\\\\SESSION_122_1.pdf", "size": null, "shown": true, "status": null, "sujetPV": null, "dateDepot": null, "dateUpload": "24-02-2025 09:29:42", "pvDocument": null, "responsable": null, "originalName": "Dissertation Anglais.pdf", "dateTelechargement": null}]	DONE	<p>The new era of emergent technologies, empowered lately by the artificial intelligence, have made our lives easier, upgraded our skills and choices and made us all connected all over the world. Smartphones, the milestone of new technologies, keep us in touch with our community, family and colleagues, drives us safely and easily through new unkown paths, reminds us of our key-dates and helps us programming and organizing all of our activities. None of us , smartphone users, is capable of dropping down his phone for few hours or even imagine his before-smartphone life. Equipped with cutting-edge features, smartphone is the daily companion in each task. Society development metrics and illetracy is now measured through the ratio of individuals connected to the internet instead of being professionnaly or technically qualified. We see children connected, toddlers and eldest ones. This over-use lately raised awarness about smartphones and technolgy being harmful and may cause addiction in case of getting over the limits of use.</p>\n<p>None of us haven't see a young child or baby holding a smartphone for hours, focused and disconnected from real-life in restaurants and public arears. It is obvious that we are undergoing an era of severe addiction to smartphones particularly among young generations. Long hours of internet browsing, social media and endless short videos, keeps us apart from many daily normal tasks, that we used to do without smartphones few years ago. Smartphone use interfere highly with basic activity such us eating, studying or just laying down for a break. This effect is widly studied , doctors and psychologists are nowadays raising awarness and highliting health and mental issues related to this excessive use. Family, personal and professional relationships are collapsing and falling down due to lack of communication and interactions. Even in a personal frame, abusing in using smartphone, makes it harder to us to keep focused and concentrated in a task, scrolling down each few minutes interrupts the workflow. Therapies are now proposed to help indivduals in their healing trip to get rid of the phone-related anxiety, some mobile applications do so by blocking all applications following a programmed schedule. We lack the ideas and the sensation of being entertained far from our phones, we lack similarly the taste of moments of happiness and joy without being captured by smartphone camera. What if someday we wake up to figure out that no internt connection exists nor smart technology is available to guide us through the day ? We lost our skills and mental resilience as human beings and become smartphone-dependant. Being connected all day long to the virtual world may also emphasize conflicts and disagreements by not facing them and finding a compromise, either in professionnal environment or personal life. One must be aware of these tools, they are built to assist us instead of ruining our lives and keep us apart from each other. The irony of "social medias" and "internet connection" that they suppressed all kind of connection and socializing. We see human real-interactions vanish from day to day as all these technologies keen emerging.</p>\n<p>Being conscious of the harm that may be caused by smartphones and new technologies, is the key-step to a wise use. Built to help us and facilitate our daily tasks doesn't essentially make these technologies addictive. But the main question is that how we can raise awarness among young individuals since they are more attracted by mobile applications ?&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>	SOUMETTRE	\N	2
